    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="23" relname="span">In my department at work we just completed a project that migrated approximately 150 users to our Active Directory Domain.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="1" relname="elaboration">It took about 2 months to complete because we have so many locations where these users work from.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="15" relname="span">I have learned so much about how important it is to include the user during any type of IT project in which their PCs are affected.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="22" relname="span">Along with this new Domain came a bunch to group policy restrictions which limited their desktop use.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="18" relname="span">They were not allowed to do the many small things that make a huge difference in our lives</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="elaboration">like adjust their screensaver, change their desktop wallpaper, etc.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="19" relname="span">Our support group got all the complaints about this,</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="7" relname="concession">even after they were all notified of these restrictions.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="20" relname="concession">A few of our programs were changed around a bit,</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="11" relname="means">but by working with the users from the beginning and gaining the knowledge of how they have certain programs configured</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="20" relname="span">we are able to duplicate this on the new system, trying to keep them satisfied.</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="15" relname="elaboration">It was a learning experience I wanted to share with the class.</segment>
        <group id="13" type="span"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="13" relname="span"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="14" relname="span"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="3" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
        <group id="18" type="span" parent="4" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="17" relname="span"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="21" relname="span"/>
        <group id="21" type="span" parent="19" relname="volitional-result"/>
        <group id="22" type="span" parent="17" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
        <group id="23" type="span" parent="14" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
    </body>
